* MKGOLD.PRG - build the dBASE III Plus reference tables.
*
* Run by mkgold.sh through rundb.sh, with D:\SEED.DBF from install.sh and
* the memo texts M1.TXT and M2.TXT in the current directory (short names:
* the 15-key BIOS buffer must hold every queued key).
*
* Creates ITEMS.DBF + ITEMS.DBT, CATS.DBF, LOANS.DBF and USERS.DBF with
* layouts modelled on the inventory schema's through CREATE ... FROM a
* structure-extended table, and appends records that cover every field type:
* negative and blank numbers, blank dates, true, false and blank
* logicals, a short memo, a memo longer than one 512-byte block followed
* by another memo, and empty memos.  One record is deleted.  ITEMS1.NDX
* indexes ITEMS on STR(ITEM_ID,8).  BIG.DBF (300 records) carries three
* larger indexes, BIG1.NDX to BIG3.NDX; NUM2000, NUM993, WIDE and WIDED
* (described where they are built) show deeper trees, wide keys and an
* index after key deletions.  A listing of every table goes to OUT.TXT.
*
* REPLACE cannot store text in a memo field in dBASE III Plus, so each
* memo is read from its text file in the memo editor: KSTUFF queues
* Ctrl-PgDn (open the memo), Ctrl-K R and the file name (read the file),
* Enter, then Ctrl-End twice (save the memo, save the record).
ON ERROR DO DBERR
SET DELETED OFF
USE D:\SEED
COPY STRUCTURE EXTENDED TO STRU
* ITEMS: 21 fields.
